<item>
            <title>[PARQUET-357] Parquet-thrift generates wrong schema for Thrift binary fields</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PARQUET-357</link>
                <project id="12315521" key="PARQUET">Parquet</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Thrift &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/thrift/blob/0.9.0/lib/java/src/org/apache/thrift/protocol/TType.java#L26-L39&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;doesn&apos;t have true &lt;tt&gt;BINARY&lt;/tt&gt; type&lt;/a&gt;. The &lt;tt&gt;BINARY&lt;/tt&gt; type is actually just an unencoded &lt;tt&gt;STRING&lt;/tt&gt;. Quoted from &lt;a href=&quot;https://thrift.apache.org/docs/types&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;Thrift Types&lt;/a&gt; section of official Thrift documentation:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;binary: a sequence of unencoded bytes&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;N.B.: This is currently a specialized form of the string type above, added to provide better interoperability with Java. The current plan-of-record is to elevate this to a base type at some point.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The consequence is that, Thrift &lt;tt&gt;BINARY&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;STRING&lt;/tt&gt; are both passed to &lt;tt&gt;parquet-thrift&lt;/tt&gt; as &lt;tt&gt;STRING&lt;/tt&gt;, and are &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/parquet-mr/blob/apache-parquet-1.7.0/parquet-thrift/src/main/java/org/apache/parquet/thrift/ThriftSchemaConvertVisitor.java#L249-L252&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;always encoded as &lt;tt&gt;BINARY (UTF8)&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is really a problem on Thrift side. One possible workaround is to inspect binary fields in the actual generated Java classes to see whether the type is &lt;tt&gt;ByteBuffer&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
